1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,110
Do you see the error?

2
00:00:02,655 --> 00:00:07,450
The documented path misses a directory — the
file lives one level deeper.

3
00:00:07,585 --> 00:00:09,990
The documented path does not exist.

4
00:00:10,175 --> 00:00:14,090
Errors like this have always existed — no
amount of care prevents them.

5
00:00:14,245 --> 00:00:19,000
What changed is the volume: more documentation
is written by AI coding agents.

6
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:23,120
A 2026 study of 612 agent configuration files

7
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:26,840
found stale references in 23% of repositories.

8
00:00:27,090 --> 00:00:29,540
Reviewing that by hand does not scale;

9
00:00:29,650 --> 00:00:33,490
asking another model just swaps a stale claim
for a guess.

10
00:00:33,805 --> 00:00:36,880
We split a document into atomic claims and
check each one

11
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:40,150
against a fact inventory built from the
repository itself.

12
00:00:40,445 --> 00:00:44,690
The verdict is discrete: SUPPORTED, REFUTED,
or NEI.

13
00:00:44,745 --> 00:00:49,210
NEI is not a confidence threshold — it means
the inventory cannot decide.

14
00:00:49,405 --> 00:00:54,910
Six predicates, one fixed inventory each: path
and Dockerfile read the file listing,

15
00:00:55,045 --> 00:00:58,670
symbol reads the Python tree, dependency reads
the manifests,

16
00:00:58,805 --> 00:01:02,830
license and CI read the license field and the
workflows directory.

17
00:01:03,085 --> 00:01:06,320
No language model sits in the deciding path.

18
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:09,370
Let's run it live on a different project.

19
00:01:09,645 --> 00:01:12,200
Paste the repository URL and clone it

20
00:01:12,270 --> 00:01:15,115
the whole analysis runs in less than a second.

21
00:01:15,363 --> 00:01:20,420
Here is the report: claims with verdicts,
coverage, five predicates.

22
00:01:20,730 --> 00:01:23,120
Exactly one claim is refuted.

23
00:01:23,440 --> 00:01:27,520
Open it: the example calls httpx.Mounts

24
00:01:27,530 --> 00:01:30,340
a class that does not exist anywhere in the
project;

25
00:01:30,440 --> 00:01:32,900
the name appears only in this document.

26
00:01:33,170 --> 00:01:37,610
This is a real divergence, confirmed against
git history.

27
00:01:37,925 --> 00:01:40,320
Now a yellow one: NEI.

28
00:01:40,510 --> 00:01:45,020
The documentation mentions asgi-lifespan; the
project does not declare it

29
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:49,420
but that is not proof it is absent, because
the dependency graph is open.

30
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:54,340
The layer and the reason are printed on the
card.

31
00:01:55,530 --> 00:01:59,800
A tool that reports findings is not yet a tool
that works

32
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:02,160
so we manufacture the defects.

33
00:02:02,430 --> 00:02:05,390
Six held-out repositories in three domains.

34
00:02:05,615 --> 00:02:08,270
We inject one drift of a known class,

35
00:02:08,395 --> 00:02:10,520
prove on disk with an engine-free oracle

36
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:13,250
that the artifact existed before and is gone
after,

37
00:02:13,345 --> 00:02:15,710
and measure the tool's reaction.

38
00:02:16,125 --> 00:02:21,770
Sixty-nine verified injections, sixty-five
detected — recall 0.942,

39
00:02:21,905 --> 00:02:26,830
confidence interval 0.873 to 0.986.

40
00:02:27,235 --> 00:02:31,660
Fifty by a closed-world refutation, fifteen by
a named abstention.

41
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:37,690
We also ran it on real, widely used projects.
Sixteen of them.

42
00:02:37,965 --> 00:02:43,520
Eight carry drift that we confirmed against
git history — 32 defects in total.

43
00:02:43,810 --> 00:02:46,230
Some of these have been wrong for years.

44
00:02:46,485 --> 00:02:51,960
In Celery, a contributing guide still points
at a file deleted in 2016.

45
00:02:52,270 --> 00:02:56,780
In SQLFluff, the path we opened with was
written in 2023

46
00:02:56,890 --> 00:02:59,620
a year after the file had already moved.

47
00:02:59,860 --> 00:03:02,100
We do not replace human review,

48
00:03:02,210 --> 00:03:05,450
and we do not guarantee that documentation is
correct.

49
00:03:05,725 --> 00:03:09,400
We find provable divergences between
documentation and code

50
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:12,260
and stay silent when the evidence is not
there.

51
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:16,850
The same facts are served to coding agents
over MCP. Open source;

52
00:03:16,985 --> 00:03:20,900
the container and the frozen corpus reproduce
every number on this screen.
